-- The let-bound sibling of observeContinuousEqualsLetfree. Binding the latent
-- routes inference through the set-valued-witnesses engine instead of the InjF
-- `hasAnyExcept` combinator. The two engines agree: the True branch reports
-- the underlying Normal's density at the compared point, and its complement
-- (`Left ()`) is the whole unit mass, since a mass minus a density is the mass
-- (task sampling-matches-pdf-continuous-equality-density, which before its
-- 2026-09-29 review had the letfree sibling answer `1 - density` there). The
-- `Right` rows' dim of 0 is not the density convention's: `observe` binds `v`
-- to a value enumerable over {0, 2}, and an enumerated sum reports a mass
-- whatever its body (task enumerated-sum-over-density-body).
main = observe (draw x = Normal in if x == 0.0 then 0 else 2) (\v -> v < 2)
